{"title":"Scotland facts of the day","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/958272113/0/marginalrevolution~Scotland-facts-of-the-day.html","date":1782112166000,"content":"<p>By one metric there are 841,000 practicing Catholics in Scotland, with 184,283 attending Mass regularly.  That puts Catholics as far outnumbering Protestants in Scotland, for the first time since the Reformation.</p>\r\n<p>Between 2012 and 2022, the number of obese adults in Scotland rose 46 percent, to comprise about one-third of the population.</p>\r\n<p>In 1950, 76 percent of Scots age 16 or older were married, now it is about 45 percent.</p>\r\n<p>All those details are from the new and fun book by Alistair Moffat, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/See-Ourselves-Personal-History-Scotland/dp/1780279477/ref=sr_1_1?crid=1NJAPYZ898SP2&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.8tiGV9Kn3HSPPyaU-ZM_vmbR2vry3mK1an3BhHfWm0D-_jAFzOqXpD3-qUSaVQh8.ziz3Pn3I_ulY65Bk9nV4yoJ87mqeMuroIwqdDMaVxuw&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=To+See+Ourselves%3A+A+Personal+History+of+Scotland+Since+1950&amp;nsdOptOutParam=true&amp;qid=1782065607&amp;sprefix=to+see+ourselves+a+personal+history+of+scotland+since+1950%2Caps%2C792&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">To See Ourselves: A Personal History of Scotland Since 1950</a>.  From these tidbits I conclude that “Scotland as we knew it” is not just evolving, but also disappearing.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/06/scotland-facts-of-the-day.html\">Scotland facts of the day</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/958272113/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/958272113/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.f